        "url": "https://mastodon.social/@gokayburuc/115966294026093918",
        "published": "2026-01-27",
        "text": "@yvg AI always selects samples at the peak of the normal distribution curve.If your sample is either at the forward or backward point in the distribution, it will not present this as the optimum solution. In other words, artificial intelligence can sometimes overlook very good examples, and sometimes it can offer overly complex solutions for very simple ones.At this point, programmers who are familiar with the systems and know what each code does have a bigger role to play."
      }
